             Chart Calculation Techniques

For this work, the Tropical Zodiac and the Placidus
House systems are used. The natal horoscope is the
main point of reference. It is occasionally referred to as
the radical chart or the radix. It occupies the inner
wheel throughout the illustrations in Part One, unaltered
in any way. This natal horoscope should be calculated
based on accurate and precise birth data including the
time, date, and location of birth. Precision is a must to
predict accurately. Even a few minutes off can cause
subsequent charts to be unreliable.

   Although it is not necessary, for purposes of
efficiency, computer calculations are recommended.
Time is valuable and several charts may be used in
conjunction in some of the following techniques.

                   Astrolo8ical CocL

Since the astrologer is human and can make mistakes in
entering data for a computer to calculate, all data should

